  "text": "We are given a semicircle with center $ O $, and the arc $ \\widehat{AB} $ has length 90 units. Segment $ AC $ is perpendicular to $ OB $, and intersects $ OB $ at point $ M $. We are also told that $ \\angle CMO = 60^\\circ $. We are to find the **area of sector $ AOB $**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Geometry\n\n- The arc $ \\widehat{AB} $ is part of a **semicircle**, so the angle $ \\angle AOB $ is a **right angle** (i.e., $ 90^\\circ $), because in a semicircle, the angle subtended by the diameter is a right angle.\n- Therefore, the sector $ AOB $ is a **quarter of a circle** (since the angle is $ 90^\\circ $, and a full circle is $ 360^\\circ $).\n- So the **area of sector $ AOB $** is $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the area of the **full circle**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the Arc Length to Find the Radius\n\nWe are given that the **arc length** $ \\widehat{AB} = 90 $ units.\n\nLet the **radius of the semicircle** be $ r $.\n\nThe arc length of a circle is given by:\n$$\n\\text{Arc length} = r \\cdot \\theta\n$$\nWhere $ \\theta $ is the central angle in **radians**.\n\nSince $ \\angle AOB = 90^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi}{2} $ radians, the arc length is:\n$$\n90 = r \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\nSolve for $ r $:\n$$\nr = \\frac{90 \\cdot 2}{\\pi} = \\frac{180}{\\pi}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the Area of the Full Circle\n\nThe area of a circle is:\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\nSo:\n$$\nA = \\pi \\left( \\frac{180}{\\pi} \\right)^2 = \\pi \\cdot \\frac{32400}{\\pi^2} = \\frac{32400}{\\pi}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Find the Area of Sector $ AOB $\n\nSince $ \\angle AOB = 90^\\circ $, the sector $ AOB $ is $ \\frac{1}{4} $ of the full circle:\n$$\n\\text{Area of sector } AOB = \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{32400}{\\pi} = \\frac{8100}{\\pi}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{8100}{\\pi}}\n$$",
